msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:90
#. Diagram label
msgid "Act on the answer"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:97
#. Diagram label
msgid "Answer acted on"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:27
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Any agent that is not the one talking with the person: a project thread, a subagent, a workflow agent, a cloud session. It did the analysis, so it composes the hand-back."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:75
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ask the person"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "By the host's route: `message_coordinator` or `message_thread` in Claude projects; the final report (a json block valid against the input schema) for a subagent; `SendMessage` for a sibling session. Then keep working on the recommended option where it can be undone, or stop if `blocking`."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:87
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Chat copies keep their text: the question struck through and \"[Edit: <letter> chosen by <who>, <time>]\" added. Cards closed with the chosen option. The sheet's \"Decision needed\" block replaced by the decision and who made it. Withdrawn or superseded hand-backs marked the same way, with the reason."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:49
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Compose it once, against the input schema: a question is the full ask-the-person input (what will differ, context, lettered options with a one-line trade-off each, the recommendation, what happens with no answer); context, a result or a blocker gets the same stand-alone test. Post it in your own thread too, chat text then card. Your own thread is never the only copy."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:48
#. Diagram label
msgid "Compose the hand-back and post it in own thread"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:37
#. Diagram label
msgid "Discussion agent"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:55
#. Diagram label
msgid "Feedback channel in play?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:14
#. Diagram label
msgid "Hand back to the discussion"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:63
#. Diagram label
msgid "Hand it back to the discussion agent"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:17
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "How a sibling agent gets a card, question, result, blocker or context in front of the person: through the discussion agent that is talking with them, never only in its own thread. The person's answer comes back the same way. INPUT AND OUTPUT: the `hand-back-to-discussion` skill's schemas, schemas/skills/hand-back-to-discussion/input.schema.json (from, to, kind, summary, ask = the ask-the-person input, context, links, channels, answerRoute, blocking) and output.schema.json (shown, state, chosen, quote, answeredIn, marked, deliveredBack). THE PERSON'S STEP is inside `Process_AskThePerson`, called by the discussion agent, so the asking rule (chat text first, then the card) holds here unchanged. A Blue-column answer in a review sheet is an answer to that same question."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:86
#. Diagram label
msgid "Mark every copy answered"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:58
#. Diagram label
msgid "Mirror it to the feedback channel"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:67
#. Diagram label
msgid "Needs an answer?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:91
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Never ask the person again for what they answered. A rule-level answer goes into the governing skill in the same turn."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:101
#. Diagram label
msgid "no"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:83
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "On `answerRoute`, with the person's own message attached by id where the host allows, so the sibling can treat it as the person's approval. A paraphrase is never approval."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:74
#. Diagram label
msgid "Person informed"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:70
#. Diagram label
msgid "Post it in the discussion"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:59
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Review sheet: the \"Decision needed\" block in the row's agent column, Agentic status `Needs you` (the document layer's `review-sheet-script` skill). Issue or PR: a comment. An extra copy, never instead of the discussion."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:82
#. Diagram label
msgid "Route the answer back, quoted"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:71
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Say it comes from the sibling (title and link) and give the context or result in full. State `informed`."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:26
#. Diagram label
msgid "Sibling"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:38
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The agent the person is talking with right now. Shows the hand-back, asks, marks every copy answered and routes the answer back."
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:47
#. Diagram label
msgid "The person must see or decide something"
msgstr ""

#: processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn:76
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The sibling's ask, unchanged in letters and recommendation, through `Process_AskThePerson`: the full chat text first, naming the sibling and that the answer will be passed on, then the card. A tap on the sibling's own card or a Blue-column answer in the sheet answers it too; take the first."
msgstr ""

